    "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Biosemi ActiveTwo 128-channel system at 1024 Hz (2048 Hz for some participants) inside a Faraday cage under dim light (120-150 lux). In a single ~20-minute session, participants completed two eyes-open and two eyes-closed 5-minute runs, with order randomly assigned. They were told to sit still and avoid muscle tension. In the eyes-open condition they looked at a black fixation point on a white wall.",
